# Normalise line endings for text, but never touch binary deliverables.
#
# core.autocrlf is enabled on this machine, and git guesses whether a file is
# text by sampling its first bytes. The ReportLab PDF has no NUL byte early on,
# so git guessed "text" and announced it would rewrite its line endings, which
# corrupts the binary streams inside the PDF on checkout. The submitted report,
# spreadsheet and database must round-trip byte for byte.

* text=auto

*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.zip   binary
*.7z    binary
*.tar   binary
*.gz    binary
*.doc   binary
*.docx  binary
*.sav   binary
*.por   binary
*.dta   binary
*.sas7bdat binary
